-- #3377: a product that overflows i64 itself, not just the 63-bit range:
-- 3037000500^2 is just past 2^63, so the wrapped i64 product is a small positive
-- number that fits 63 bits.  Only $mdk_int_mul's second check (`p / a == b`) can
-- see it, so this pins that check.
-- expect-stderr: runtime error [E-INT-OVERFLOW]: 3037000500 * 3037000500 overflows Int
main = 3037000500 * 3037000500
